CORE broken-smt-backend no-new-smt wide-pointer-encoding
main.c
--wide-pointer-encoding
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deref into pointer-containing global is sound: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A pointer-containing global reached via an opaque integer address is skipped
as an address-dispatch candidate in value_set_dereferencet, but is still
resolved by the solver's backward-constraint refinement: the pointer field is
read precisely (== &x). See main-violation.c for the violation direction.
